          <div class="section_title mb-4">
            <h2>Solution</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Aims to establish student assessments as foundation for education reform, addressing each child's learning needs. It envisions creating an assessment cell to reform systems and processes by strengthening institutions, stakeholders, and middle management through: </p>
          <ul class="list">
            <li><b>System Strengthening:</b> Establish specialized units with cascade model, building infrastructure to design and implement 360-degree practices, establishing project management unit (PMU’s) for effective governance and sustainability </li>
            <li><b>People Strengthening Developing</b> capacity building curriculum for assessment cadre on 21st cc assessments, developing subject matter experts for implementation future ready assessments, setting up Professional Learning Communities (PLC’s) through Live Action Plan (LAP’s) </li>
            <li><b>Tech Integration:</b> Tech enabled processed for driving learner-centric insights for policy making, MLE systems to ensure transparency and reliability of reforms, and developing assessment portals as warehouse of 21st cc domain assessment tools </li>
            <li><b>Holistic Product Integration:</b> Integrating Holistic progress card (HPC) to include cognitive, affective and psychomotor domains furthering a whole child development approach to student assessment, using School-based assessment (SBA) to serve as key lever in realising this vision. </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
