            <h2>Impact</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Has successfully created partnerships with government stakeholders across 4 states - Rajasthan, J&K, Odisha and Jharkhand - supporting across institutional, process refinement and capacity building aspects.</p>
          <ul class="list">
            <li><strong>Creation of Assessment Cell and resource persons -</strong> States (Rajasthan, Jharkhand, Odisha) successfully influenced to establish Assessment cells </li>
            <li><strong>Capacity building workshops -</strong> Supported state government in conducting capacity building workshops on School Based Assessments (SBA), Holistic Progress cards (HPC) impacting 3.11 lakh teachers in Rajasthan and 1.7 lakh in Odisha </li>
            <li><strong>Large Scale Assessments -</strong> Supported Odisha in conducting Large Scale Assessments, assessed 1.16L+ students’ learning levels, identify learning gaps, needs to better target state education strategies </li>
            <li><strong>Unlocking INR Budget for assessment reform initiatives -</strong> Unlocked 67 Cr budget in Rajasthan through Strengthening Teaching-Learning and Results for States (STARS), Project Approval Board (PAB), 1.5 Cr in Odisha, 2.5 Cr in Jharkhand </li>
            <li><strong>Resource Person (RP) selection and capacity building -</strong> Assisted in creating and executing selection process for assessments cadre. State and District level Resource Persons’ capacity building done - 81 in Rajasthan, 120 in Jharkhand, and 65 in Odisha </li>
            <li><strong>Establishing Digital Infrastructure for Assessments -</strong> The Rajasthan State Assessment Cell has developed an assessment portal containing a repository of 10,000+ learning outcome-based test items and various other resources that can be accessed by teachers across Rajasthan benefitting 60 lakh students </li>
            <li><strong>Amulya - </strong>Amulya like skills assessment provides a snapshot on life skills health of students and system preparedness among teachers and system officials to ensure effective delivery of life skills education. Completed across four states-Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Jammu &amp; Kashmir, and Jharkhand reaching a total of 3,04,000 children </li>
          </ul>
